// A model GenMC cannot explore, which Kater exports all the same.
//
// The acyclicity constraint orders a thread's writes, and its reads, but
// ppo does not: a revisit keeps a write without the writes po-before it,
// and GenMC adds those later, into the hole. In message passing,
//
//     x := 1;  y := 1;  ||  a := y;  b := x;
//
// once y := 1 has revisited a := y (a = 1) and b := x has read 0, x := 1
// cannot be added: b -fr-> x := 1 -[W];po;[W]-> y := 1 -rfe-> a -[R];po;[R]-> b
// is a cycle, and x := 1 has no other place in mo. The model is not
// extensible (mp.graph, kater-oracle extensible), like the formulation of
// POWER in MP-EXT of Kokologiannakis's thesis (section 5.4.1). Kater used to
// export it, as isPPOIntersectionInPPO decided nothing (vzhn/kater-fork#33);
// it rejects it now, at the [W];po;[W] step out of x := 1.

let ppo = data | addr | ctrl

view hb = po
export coherence hb

export acyclic (ppo | rfe | mo | fr | [W];po;[W] | [R];po;[R] | tc | tj | lin)
